          {
            "icon": "✍️",
            "label": "Spelling stayed",
            "cue": "spelling"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Why didn't the spelling change too?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Spelling often changes more slowly than talking. So the old K stayed in the word, like a little fossil!",
      "punch": "fossil",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🦴",
        "text": "A spelling fossil",
        "cue": "fossil",
        "sub": "Old letter, no sound",
        "sub_cue": "old"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Are there more silent K words?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Lots! Knee, knock, know and knot all start with a silent K.",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Silent K words",
